From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:46:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] libcss: CSS custom properties and var()

- The lexer reads --name as an identifier (CSS Syntax 3).
- The parser keeps a custom property (--name: tokens) and any
  declaration whose value uses var() as text (CSS_OP_CUSTOM_PROPERTY,
  CSS_OP_VAR_DECLARATION).
- Selection collects them with their origin, importance, specificity
  and order; after the node's cascade (select/custom.c) its custom
  properties are its parent's plus its own (var() in their values
  substituted; cycles and missing names make a property undefined;
  inherit, unset, initial), kept on the computed style for the children,
  and each var() declaration is substituted, parsed as an inline style
  (cached per selection context) and cascaded with its own weight; an
  equal ordinary declaration that came later still wins; one that fails
  is unset.  Shorthands, fallbacks and nested var() work.
- autogenerated_computed.h gets the custom_properties pointer by hand
  (select_generator.py does not know it yet).
